git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "Mapping Review: show the decision pipeline in both views. The tool resolves every field through an ordered stack - approved golden record first, then learned rules, then an uploaded mapping workbook, then rules you applied by hand, then deterministic matches (country/currency/UOM/flags + name match), then constant defaults, and only where none of those had an answer does AI fill the gap. That precedence was real in the engine but invisible in the UI. New PrecedenceBar sits above both the canvas and the table: it names the seven layers in priority order with a LIVE count of how many of this conversion's fields each one carried, a one-line 'highest layer wins, AI fills the rest' explainer, the % that fell through to AI, and an expandable full description of each layer. Refactored the per-field classifier into one shared taxonomy (classifyLayer + LAYER_META) so the bar, the table's 'How it's mapped' column, and the new canvas per-field layer badge can never disagree - the canvas cards previously showed only a confidence pill and now carry the same Golden record / Learned / Mapping workbook / Your rule / Deterministic / Default / AI badge the table has. Layer origin is read precisely from the reason string the learning engine stamps (captured from gold example / mapping workbook / metadata catalog), verified across all layers including the case where a workbook rule's reason also mentions the learning library."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
